3. BUILD ATTEMPTS AND FAILURE MODES (root causes + fixes)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Attempt 1  (21:04:39Z, log: logs/p2_path_a_build.log first section)
  FAIL: libffi recipe -> ./autogen.sh -> "exec: autoreconf: not found"
  ROOT CAUSE: host has no autoconf/automake/libtool (and no m4).
  FIX (applied): local recipe override tools/local-recipes/libffi/ that downloads
       the libffi RELEASE tarball (ships a pre-generated ./configure) and skips
       autogen.sh/autoreconf — this is what the shipped, proven PATH-A build uses.

  FOLLOW-UP FINDING (C1 asked for the autotools-from-source route; now COMPLETE):
       GNU autotools build cleanly non-root into android/spike/tools/autotools
       (script android/spike/build_autotools.sh, log logs/autotools_build.log):
         m4 1.4.21 -> autoconf 2.72 -> automake 1.17 (aclocal 1.17) -> libtool 2.4.7
       KEY DETAIL: m4 1.4.19 (my first attempt) does NOT compile on this host's
       gcc/glibc (gnulib error in gl_oset.h); m4 1.4.20/1.4.21 do. Its configure
       needs m4 already on PATH — the built prefix supplies it for the later pkgs.
       VERIFIED END-TO-END: with that prefix on PATH, the STOCK p4a libffi recipe
       flow succeeds on a pristine checkout —
         libffi v3.4.2 git archive (no ./configure) -> apply remove-version-info.patch
         -> autoreconf -vif -> rc=0, ./configure generated, -avoid-version present.
       => with autotools present the libffi override is NOT needed. (A host with
       neither autotools nor the override still fails at libffi, as first observed.)
       NOTE: the second override (android --no-isolation) is needed REGARDLESS —
       it is a pip build-isolation issue, unrelated to autotools.

Attempt 2  (21:15:07Z)
  FAIL: IsADirectoryError: '.p4a'  (p4a reads a config file named .p4a in its cwd)
  ROOT CAUSE: storage dir was named <cwd>/.p4a -> collided with p4a's config file.
  FIX: storage dir moved to android/spike/.p4a-storage (outside cwd);

Attempt 3  (21:17:02Z)
  FAIL: android recipe -> Python build backend -> "No module named 'Cython'"
  ROOT CAUSE: p4a's internal 'android' recipe builds with pip build ISOLATION and
              its setup.py imports Cython at import time; the isolated env only
              gets setuptools. (p4a installs Cython into the host env via
              hostpython_prerequisites, but isolation hides it.)
  FIX: local recipe override tools/local-recipes/android/ with
       extra_build_args = ['--no-isolation'] (copied from the built-in recipe so
       its IncludedFilesBehaviour 'src' dir resolves).

Attempt 4  (21:29:06Z -> 21:31:03Z)
  SUCCESS. p4a apk reported: "# Android package renamed to dkbt_path_a-debug-0.1.apk"
  PATH_A_BUILD_SECONDS=117  (warm recipe cache; recipes hostpython3/libffi/
  openssl/sqlite3/python3/flask/pyjnius/android already built)

