6. DEVICE-PROOF CONSTRAINT (environment limitation, recorded for R1)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The brief's suggested proof commands are all unavailable in this environment:
  - `waydroid logcat`          -> "needs root access"
  - `waydroid shell`           -> "needs root access"
  - `grim` (wlr-screencopy)    -> "compositor doesn't support wlr-screencopy-unstable-v1"
  - GNOME D-Bus Screenshot / ScreenshotWindow / Introspect -> "AccessDenied: not allowed"
  - `waydroid adb connect`     -> "Unknown container IP address" (bridge 192.168.240.1/24 up,
                                  container has NO IPv4 lease; ARP 192.168.240.112 FAILED)
WORKING METHOD (used): restart the Waydroid UI client so its window is on top, then
  `flameshot full -p <png>` (flameshot is the only working Wayland screen grabber here).
  helper: android/spike/capture_ui.sh ; used by android/spike/run_on_waydroid.sh
NOTE: flameshot captures the whole screen, so the Waydroid window must be in front;
      the first probe capture (full desktop) was overwritten — no desktop content kept.

